// Runtime-correctness regression for DL-067b: the DADAO backend registered
// ISD::BR_CC lowering in two places (LowerOperation via Custom + a redundant
// PerformDAGCombine target-combine that fired pre-legalize and could convert
// an illegal-typed br_cc into an opaque DADAOISD:: node before type
// legalization could promote it -- "Do not know how to promote this
// operator's operand!"). This is the exact alignment-check + early-NUL-scan
// shape (from libc string functions) that triggered it. Dual-backend checks
// four distinct branch outcomes (aligned-skip / full-walk / early-NUL at two
// trip counts), not just "compiles without crashing".
// RUN: %llvm-mc -triple=dadao -filetype=obj -o %t.crt0.o %S/../../scripts/crt0.s
// RUN: %clang --target=dadao-unknown-elf -nostdlib -Wl,-T,%S/../../scripts/dadao.ld %t.crt0.o %S/Inputs/align_strfn.c -o %t.elf
// RUN: %llvm-objcopy -O binary %t.elf %t.bin
// RUN: bash -c '%qemu -M dadao-m1 -nographic -bios %trampoline -kernel %t.bin >/dev/null 2>&1; test $? -eq 0'
// RUN: bash -c '%gem5 %gem5_se %t.elf >/dev/null 2>&1; test $? -eq 0'
